---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'SSI Eligibility Checker for the Bronx (2026)';
const meta = 'Quick eligibility checker for Supplemental Security Income (SSI) based on income, assets, age, and disability. Federal limits, New York supplement, and what to do next.';
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebApplication", "name": "SSI Eligibility Checker", "applicationCategory": "FinanceApplication", "operatingSystem": "Web" };
---
<Base title={title} description={meta} schema={schema}>
  <section class="container-narrow tool-page">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to home</a>
    <span class="eyebrow">Free tool</span>
    <h1>SSI Eligibility Checker</h1>
    <p class="lead">Quick check whether you might qualify for <strong>Supplemental Security Income (SSI)</strong> based on the basic federal rules. This tool is informational only — the SSA makes the final determination. New York State adds a small supplement on top of the federal amount.</p>

    <div class="tool-box">
      <form id="ssi-form" class="tool-form" onsubmit="return false;">
        <div class="field">
          <label>Are you applying as an individual or a couple?</label>
          <div class="radio-row">
            <label class="radio-pill"><input type="radio" name="status" value="individual" checked> Individual</label>
            <label class="radio-pill"><input type="radio" name="status" value="couple"> Couple</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label>Which category applies to you?</label>
          <div class="radio-col">
            <label class="radio-pill"><input type="radio" name="category" value="age" checked> Age 65 or older</label>
            <label class="radio-pill"><input type="radio" name="category" value="disabled"> Disabled (medically determined)</label>
            <label class="radio-pill"><input type="radio" name="category" value="blind"> Blind (statutorily blind)</label>
            <label class="radio-pill"><input type="radio" name="category" value="child"> Child under 18 with disability</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="income">Monthly income before taxes (all sources)</label>
          <div class="input-with-prefix">
            <span class="prefix">$</span>
            <input type="number" id="income" name="income" min="0" placeholder="0" />
          </div>
          <p class="help">Wages, Social Security, pensions, unemployment, child support — include everything. For couples, include both incomes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="assets">Total countable resources (assets)</label>
          <div class="input-with-prefix">
            <span class="prefix">$</span>
            <input type="number" id="assets" name="assets" min="0" placeholder="0" />
          </div>
          <p class="help">Cash, bank accounts, stocks, second properties, additional vehicles. Your primary home and one vehicle generally do NOT count.</p>
        </div>

        <button type="button" id="check-btn" class="btn btn-blue">Check eligibility</button>
      </form>

      <div id="result" class="result hidden"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>How the SSI rules work in 2024</h2>
      <p>Supplemental Security Income is a needs-based federal program for people who are <strong>disabled, blind, or age 65 or older</strong>, and who have very limited income and resources. Unlike SSDI, it does not require any work history.</p>

      <h3>The asset limits</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Individual:</strong> countable resources generally must be below <strong>$2,000</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Couple:</strong> countable resources generally must be below <strong>$3,000</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Your primary home, one vehicle, household goods, burial plots, and certain other items do NOT count toward the limit. Cash, additional vehicles, second properties, and investment accounts DO count.</p>

      <h3>The federal maximum benefit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Individual:</strong> up to about <strong>$943/month</strong> federal payment in 2024.</li>
        <li><strong>Couple:</strong> up to about <strong>$1,415/month</strong> federal payment in 2024.</li>
        <li><strong>New York supplement:</strong> small additional amount on top, varies by living arrangement.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How income reduces SSI</h3>
      <p>Most income reduces SSI almost dollar-for-dollar after small monthly exclusions. Earned income (wages) is treated more favorably than unearned income (pensions, gifts). In-kind support — such as free housing or food from family — also reduces SSI.</p>

      <h3>What happens if you qualify</h3>
      <p>In New York, SSI eligibility generally conveys automatic Medicaid eligibility, which is one of the most important practical benefits. New York is a 1634 state, meaning you do not need to apply separately for Medicaid in most cases.</p>

      <h3>Disclaimer</h3>
      <p>This tool uses the basic federal eligibility rules to give a quick estimate. The SSA makes the final determination based on a detailed review of your specific situation, including any deductions, exclusions, and household composition rules. Get the full process at <a href="/apply-for-ssi-bronx/">how to apply for SSI in the Bronx</a> or visit <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/ssi/">ssa.gov/ssi</a> for the official application.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <h3>Ready to apply for SSI?</h3>
      <p>Start the application online at ssa.gov, by phone at 1-800-772-1213, or in person at any of the five Bronx SSA offices.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/apply-for-ssi-bronx/" class="btn btn-blue">How to apply (full guide)</a>
        <a href="/social-security-office-bronx/" class="btn btn-ghost">Find a Bronx office</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
(function(){
  const FEDERAL_INDIVIDUAL = 943;
  const FEDERAL_COUPLE = 1415;
  const RESOURCE_LIMIT_INDIVIDUAL = 2000;
  const RESOURCE_LIMIT_COUPLE = 3000;
  const NY_SUPPLEMENT_INDIVIDUAL = 87;
  const NY_SUPPLEMENT_COUPLE = 104;
  const GENERAL_INCOME_EXCLUSION = 20;
  const EARNED_INCOME_EXCLUSION = 65;

  document.getElementById('check-btn').addEventListener('click', function(){
    const status = document.querySelector('input[name="status"]:checked').value;
    const category = document.querySelector('input[name="category"]:checked').value;
    const income = parseFloat(document.getElementById('income').value) || 0;
    const assets = parseFloat(document.getElementById('assets').value) || 0;

    const isCouple = status === 'couple';
    const federalMax = isCouple ? FEDERAL_COUPLE : FEDERAL_INDIVIDUAL;
    const nySupplement = isCouple ? NY_SUPPLEMENT_COUPLE : NY_SUPPLEMENT_INDIVIDUAL;
    const resourceLimit = isCouple ? RESOURCE_LIMIT_COUPLE : RESOURCE_LIMIT_INDIVIDUAL;

    const result = document.getElementById('result');
    result.classList.remove('hidden');

    // Asset check
    if (assets > resourceLimit) {
      result.innerHTML = `
        <div class="result-card result-no">
          <span class="result-tag">Likely not eligible</span>
          <h3>Resources above the limit</h3>
          <p>Your reported countable resources of <strong>$${assets.toLocaleString()}</strong> exceed the SSI limit of <strong>$${resourceLimit.toLocaleString()}</strong> for a${isCouple ? ' couple' : 'n individual'}. SSI requires resources at or below this limit.</p>
          <p class="result-note">Remember: your primary home and one vehicle generally do NOT count toward this limit. If your $${assets.toLocaleString()} figure includes those, recalculate excluding them.</p>
        </div>
      `;
      result.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'nearest'});
      return;
    }

    // Income check - simplified SSI countable income
    // Subtract general exclusion ($20) from unearned income first
    // Assume mixed income: apply general exclusion
    let countableIncome = Math.max(0, income - GENERAL_INCOME_EXCLUSION);
    const estimatedBenefit = Math.max(0, federalMax - countableIncome);

    if (estimatedBenefit <= 0) {
      result.innerHTML = `
        <div class="result-card result-no">
          <span class="result-tag">Likely not eligible</span>
          <h3>Income too high</h3>
          <p>Your reported monthly income of <strong>$${income.toLocaleString()}</strong> reduces the SSI benefit to zero. The federal SSI maximum is $${federalMax}/month for a${isCouple ? ' couple' : 'n individual'}, and most income reduces SSI dollar-for-dollar after a small exclusion.</p>
          <p class="result-note">If a substantial portion of your income comes from wages (earned income), the actual SSI calculation is more favorable. Apply through the SSA for a precise determination.</p>
        </div>
      `;
      result.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'nearest'});
      return;
    }

    const totalMonthly = estimatedBenefit + nySupplement;
    const annualTotal = totalMonthly * 12;
    const catLabel = {age: 'age 65 or older', disabled: 'disability', blind: 'statutory blindness', child: 'childhood disability'}[category];

    result.innerHTML = `
      <div class="result-card result-yes">
        <span class="result-tag">Likely eligible</span>
        <h3>You may qualify for SSI</h3>
        <p>Based on your inputs (${isCouple ? 'couple' : 'individual'}, ${catLabel}, $${income}/mo income, $${assets} in resources), you appear to meet the basic SSI requirements.</p>
        <div class="result-numbers">
          <div class="num-box"><span class="num-label">Estimated federal benefit</span><span class="num-val">$${estimatedBenefit.toFixed(0)}/mo</span></div>
          <div class="num-box"><span class="num-label">NY State supplement</span><span class="num-val">+$${nySupplement}/mo</span></div>
          <div class="num-box num-total"><span class="num-label">Estimated total</span><span class="num-val">$${totalMonthly.toFixed(0)}/mo</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="result-note"><strong>Approximately $${annualTotal.toLocaleString(undefined, {maximumFractionDigits:0})} per year</strong>, plus automatic Medicaid eligibility in New York. This is an estimate based on simplified federal rules — the SSA makes the final determination.</p>
        <p>Next step: <a href="/apply-for-ssi-bronx/">read the full guide to applying for SSI in the Bronx</a>.</p>
      </div>
    `;
    result.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'nearest'});
  });
})();
</script>

<style>
  .tool-page { padding: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-9); }
  .back-link { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-5); font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--color-ink); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.2rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-7); }
  .lead strong { color: var(--color-ink); }
  .tool-box { background: var(--color-surface); border: 2.5px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: var(--space-7); box-shadow: var(--shadow-hard); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .tool-form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-6); }
  .field label { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: var(--color-ink); }
  .field .help { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-top: var(--space-2); margin-bottom: 0; }
  .radio-row { display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .radio-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .radio-pill { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2); padding: 12px 18px; border: 2px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-pill); font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.12s; background: var(--color-surface); user-select: none; }
  .radio-pill:hover { background: var(--color-yellow); }
  .radio-pill input { margin: 0; accent-color: var(--color-primary); }
  .radio-pill:has(input:checked) { background: var(--color-primary); color: #fff; border-color: var(--color-primary); }
  .input-with-prefix { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .prefix { position: absolute; left: 16px; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); pointer-events: none; }
  input[type="number"] { width: 100%; padding: 14px 16px 14px 36px; border: 2px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; background: var(--color-bg); color: var(--color-ink); }
  input[type="number"]:focus { outline: 3px solid var(--color-primary); outline-offset: 2px; }
  #check-btn { align-self: flex-start; font-size: 1.05rem; padding: 16px 32px; }
  .result.hidden { display: none; }
  .result-card { margin-top: var(--space-6); padding: var(--space-6); border: 2.5px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-md); box-shadow: var(--shadow-hard-sm); }
  .result-yes { background: var(--color-yellow); }
  .result-no { background: var(--color-bg-alt); }
  .result-tag { display: inline-block; padding: 4px 12px; border: 2px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-pill); font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--color-ink); color: #fff; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .result-yes .result-tag { background: var(--color-success); }
  .result-card h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .result-numbers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); margin: var(--space-5) 0; }
  .num-box { padding: var(--space-4); background: var(--color-surface); border: 2px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-md); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1); }
  .num-label { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .num-val { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .num-total { background: var(--color-ink); color: #fff; }
  .num-total .num-label { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); }
  .num-total .num-val { color: var(--color-yellow); }
  .result-note { font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .result-note strong { color: var(--color-ink); }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .content-section h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-4); }
  .content-section h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-3); }
  .content-section p { line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .content-section ul { padding-left: var(--space-5); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .content-section li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); line-height: 1.7; }
  .cta-box { background: var(--color-primary); color: #fff; border: 2.5px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: var(--space-6); box-shadow: var(--shadow-hard); text-align: center; }
  .cta-box h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; color: #fff; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .cta-box p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); margin-bottom: var(--space-5); }
  .cta-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cta-box .btn-ghost { background: transparent; color: #fff; border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); box-shadow: none; }
  .cta-box .btn-ghost:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); color: #fff; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .tool-box { padding: var(--space-5); }
    .result-numbers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
